{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass: the one crushed</b> — one who has no strength, for he is lowly; therefore He is a stronghold in straits, according to its meaning: in straits, crushed. And Rabbi Dunash interpreted it as a singular form from words of stronghold. And this is not the sense of the psalm."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:42.773491752Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}